Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• Track.Milliseconds: needed to convert milliseconds → minutes and decide whether the track is Short / Medium / Long.  
• Track.TrackId: joins Track with InvoiceLine to attach revenue.  
• Track.Name (optional): handy to look at real titles while exploring.  
• InvoiceLine.TrackId: foreign key that links every sold track back to the Track table.  
• InvoiceLine.UnitPrice: price charged for one unit of that track (part of revenue).  
• InvoiceLine.Quantity: how many units were bought (part of revenue).  

Typical filter / calculation conditions we may use  
• Minutes  = Milliseconds / 60000.0  
• CASE WHEN Minutes < 3 THEN 'Short'  
        WHEN Minutes BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'  
        ELSE 'Long' END AS Category  
• Revenue  = UnitPrice * Quantity  
• GROUP BY Category to aggregate min‑minutes, max‑minutes, and total revenue.

Below are ten exploratory SQLite queries (all capped at 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final logic.  
Every query is preceded by a brief comment.

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at the raw duration data for the first 20 tracks
SELECT DISTINCT "TrackId", "Milliseconds"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;

-- 2. Convert milliseconds to minutes for the same sample of tracks
SELECT DISTINCT "TrackId",
       ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;

-- 3. Derive the Short/Medium/Long bucket only, to verify the CASE logic
SELECT DISTINCT
       CASE 
           WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) < 3 THEN 'Short'
           WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE 'Long'
       END AS "LengthCategory"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;

-- 4. Inspect invoice‑line facts: price, quantity, and the track they belong to
SELECT DISTINCT "InvoiceLineId",
       "TrackId",
       "UnitPrice",
       "Quantity"
FROM "InvoiceLine"
LIMIT 20;

-- 5. Compute revenue at the invoice‑line level (price * quantity)
SELECT DISTINCT "TrackId",
       ("UnitPrice" * "Quantity") AS "Revenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine"
LIMIT 20;

-- 6. Join Track with its sales lines to see duration beside monetary info
SELECT DISTINCT t."TrackId",
       t."Milliseconds",
       il."UnitPrice",
       il."Quantity"
FROM "Track"      AS t
JOIN "InvoiceLine" AS il ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
LIMIT 20;

-- 7. Bring together category and revenue for a small joined sample
SELECT DISTINCT
       CASE 
           WHEN (t."Milliseconds" / 60000.0) < 3 THEN 'Short'
           WHEN (t."Milliseconds" / 60000.0) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'
           ELSE 'Long'
       END AS "Category",
       (il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "Revenue"
FROM "Track"       AS t
JOIN "InvoiceLine" AS il ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
LIMIT 20;

-- 8. Make sure the possible buckets are really just Short / Medium / Long
SELECT DISTINCT "Category"
FROM (
    SELECT CASE 
             WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) < 3 THEN 'Short'
             WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'
             ELSE 'Long'
           END AS "Category"
    FROM "Track"
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 9. Get the minimum track length (in minutes) found in each bucket
SELECT DISTINCT "Category",
       MIN("Minutes") AS "MinMinutes"
FROM (
    SELECT ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) AS "Minutes",
           CASE 
               WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) < 3 THEN 'Short'
               WHEN ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'
               ELSE 'Long'
           END AS "Category"
    FROM "Track"
)
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;

--10. Final combined query: min‑minutes, max‑minutes, and total revenue per category
SELECT DISTINCT
       "Category",
       MIN("Minutes") AS "MinMinutes",
       MAX("Minutes") AS "MaxMinutes",
       SUM("Revenue") AS "TotalRevenue"
FROM (
    SELECT t."TrackId",
           (t."Milliseconds" / 60000.0) AS "Minutes",
           CASE 
               WHEN (t."Milliseconds" / 60000.0) < 3 THEN 'Short'
               WHEN (t."Milliseconds" / 60000.0) BETWEEN 3 AND 5 THEN 'Medium'
               ELSE 'Long'
           END AS "Category",
           (il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity") AS "Revenue"
    FROM "Track"       AS t
    JOIN "InvoiceLine" AS il ON t."TrackId" = il."TrackId"
)
GROUP BY "Category"
LIMIT 20;
```
